# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE REMOVING A LINE. The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` in the
# builder stage and then `COPY --from=builder /app /app` into the runtime
# stage, so ANYTHING that reaches the build context is baked into the
# published production image and ships to Fly. This file is the only thing
# standing between a local scratch file and the deployed container.
#
# It is also NOT the same list as .gitignore. A path being gitignored says
# nothing about whether Docker sees it; the two have to be kept in step by
# hand, and the expensive mistakes have all been things that were gitignored
# and assumed to be safe.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and real user data. Never in the image, at any size.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Downloaded PRODUCTION database snapshots (see the "inspect prod backup"
# workflow) plus whatever else gets dropped here while debugging. These are
# full copies of the live DB: emails, password hashes, private messages, DMs,
# IP logs, dates of birth. They were reaching the image until 2026-07-31 and
# were also ~77MB of the 201MB build context.
backups/
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*.sqlite.gz
# Google OAuth client-secret JSON as downloaded from the Cloud Console. The
# server reads its credentials from env/Fly secrets, never from a file, so a
# copy in the tree is a stray credential with no reason to travel.
client_secret_*.json
**/.env
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local dev state. The deployed server keeps all of this on the Fly volume
# at /data, so the repo copy is dev-only noise (a local DB, locally uploaded
# images, crash logs from this machine).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
apps/server/data/
**/data/*.sqlite*
**/data/*.shm
**/data/*.wal
**/crash-log.jsonl*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source artwork that no longer ships. The splash backgrounds are served
# exclusively as .webp / .avif (styles.css `.splash-bg-*`, the index.html
# preload, and defaultShellBgCss in lib/theme.ts all reference those two
# extensions only); these JPGs are the originals kept in git for re-export.
# ~6MB of a 117MB context that nothing can ever request.
#
# NOT a blanket *.jpg: the_spire_og.jpg is the OpenGraph card and
# assets/themes/parchment/parchment_texture_grey.jpg is a live CSS
# background. Both must keep shipping.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
apps/web/public/the_spire_bg.jpg
apps/web/public/the_spire_bg_dark.jpg
apps/web/public/the_spire_bg_classic.jpg
apps/web/public/the_spire_bg_classic_dark.jpg
apps/web/public/the_spire_bg_old.jpg
apps/web/public/the_spire_bg_old2.jpg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests and typecheck caches. Neither is run in the image; the server boots
# straight into tsx.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
apps/server/test/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Item-icon thumbnails. Derived from the art next to them and regenerated by
# the web build inside the image, so uploading a local copy would add ~213
# files to the context for nothing. Keeping them OUT is the point: the whole
# reason they are built rather than committed is to shrink icon payloads
# without growing the deploy.
apps/web/public/assets/items/thumbs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and dependencies. Both are regenerated inside the image:
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` restores node_modules, and
# `pnpm --filter @thekeep/web run build` produces apps/web/dist.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
.git
.gitignore
*.log
/tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working notes and scratch. None of it is read at build or run time.
# `plan.md` / `plan_ext.md` are rotating scratch files, `updates.md` is the
# local player-facing log, `commit.md` is the pending changelog.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
plan.md
plan_ext.md
feature-scope.md
updates.md
commit.md
docs/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py
.claude/
README.md
phpMyChat

# Local-only junk that should never enter the Docker build context.
.tmp-*
*:Zone.Identifier
